{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:94011","published":"2026-11-02T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-03T12:15:02.399920974Z","related":["CVE-2026-19630","CVE-2026-19662","CVE-2026-94300","CVE-2026-96888","CVE-2026-97313"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-19630","CVE-2026-19662","CVE-2026-94300","CVE-2026-96888","CVE-2026-97313"],"summary":"Important: bind9.16 security update","details":"The Berkeley Internet Name Domain (BIND) is an implementation of the Domain Name System (DNS) protocols. BIND includes a DNS server (named); a resolver library (routines for applications to use when interfacing with DNS); and tools for verifying that the DNS server is operating correctly.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * bind9: bind: BIND 9: Denial of Service via crafted DNSSEC responses (CVE-2026-19662)\n  * bind: BIND: Denial of Service via unbounded processing of crafted DNS messages (CVE-2026-19630)\n  * bind: bind: Arbitrary code execution via GSS-TSIG UDP message replay (CVE-2026-94300)\n  * bind: bind: Denial of Service via assertion failure during redirect processing (CVE-2026-96888)\n  * bind: bind: Denial of service via assertion failure in RPZ query processing (CVE-2026-97313)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bind9.16","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/bind9.16"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"32:9.16.23-0.22.el8_10.21"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:94011.json"}},{"package":{"name":"bind9.16-chroot","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/bind9.16-chroot"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"32:9.16.23-0.22.el8_10.21"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/ma